Let me see the full decode.c file, particularly the parts that were truncated. Let me look at the `tacacs_decode_args` function more carefully. The vulnerability is a "Global-buffer-overflow READ 1". Let me look at the `tacacs_decode_args` function.

In `tacacs_decode_args`:
```c
uint8_t buffer[256];
...
if (arg_list[i] < 2) goto next; /* skip malformed */
if (p + arg_list[i] > end) { ... return -1; }
memcpy(buffer, p, arg_list[i]);
buffer[arg_list[i]] = '\0';
```

`arg_list[i]` is a `uint8_t`, so it can be up to 255. `buffer` is 256 bytes. `memcpy(buffer, p, arg_list[i])` copies up to 255 bytes, then `buffer[arg_list[i]] = '\0'` writes at index up to 255. That's fine since buffer is 256.

Wait, but the global-buffer-overflow READ 1... Let me look at the `fr_struct_from_network` call and the struct decoder. Actually, let me look at the `fr_tacacs_body_xor` function in base.c.

